Deviations from bash

GENERAL

- SIGQUIT and other terminating signals do not print a "Quit" or "core dumped" message
	- The correct way to do it would be using strsignal() but this is not allowed
- No \
- No && || and ( )
- No ;
- No *
- No & (or Ctrl-Z or fg)
- No local vars
- No accurate syntax errors (just a general syntax error)
- No keeping stdin open if a " or ' is not closed (just syntax error)
- Ctrl+Z puts shell to background (normal shells do not allow this)

BUILTINS

- echo only accepts -n, does not accept -nn, does not accept any other - option
- A pipeline ending with exit prints "exit"
	- The planned implementation is to never print exit at all
	- We can also just keep it like this
- pwd ignores symlinks
- cd does not update $PWD or $OLDPWD
- cd - does not work
- ~ is not expanded

HEREDOC

- << EOF allows quitting in the middle of a line with Ctrl+D (bash does not allow this)
- << EOF does not print any warning when quitting with Ctrl+D
	- Detail + hard to do so, whatever
- << EOF cat does not print a newline after ending a heredoc with Ctrl+D on an empty line
- " and ' only stop expansion in heredocs if they are explicitly contained in the limiter ("'EOF" but not "EOF")
- << $USER limiter is expanded envar, not original $USER string

ENVAR

- $"ENVAR" still prints the $
- $2 etc... do not work
- Envars are not split according to IFS
- $PWD $OLDPWD $UID $SHLVL and some other envars not managed by shell
